"""Synthetic BMW Group CTO job description for testing JD extraction (Stage C1).

Designed to produce 10-14 extractable requirements spanning: experience depth,
scope, technical (EV/SDV), industry (premium automotive), geographic (EMEA+APAC),
leadership context (digital transformation, post-acquisition), qualification
(MBA, languages), and behavioral (stakeholder navigation, consensus culture).
"""

BMW_CTO_JD_TEXT: str = """
BMW Group — Chief Technology Officer (CTO), Mobility & Digital Services

Location: Munich, Germany (with regular travel to EMEA and APAC technology centres)
Reports to: Board of Management, Member for Development
Direct reports: ~250 engineers and product managers across 4 divisions

About the Role

BMW Group is seeking a Chief Technology Officer to lead the next chapter of our
technology strategy as we accelerate the transition from a premium vehicle manufacturer
to a software-defined mobility company. The CTO will own the end-to-end technology
roadmap spanning electric vehicle (EV) architecture, software-defined vehicle (SDV)
platforms, connected services, and advanced driver-assistance systems (ADAS). This is
a Board-minus-one position with full P&L accountability for the Technology & Digital
Services division (~EUR 550M annual budget).

The successful candidate will join BMW Group at a pivotal moment: we are integrating
the recently acquired Autonomy.AI team (180 engineers, Tel Aviv & Shenzhen) into our
core R&D organisation while simultaneously executing the NEUE KLASSE programme — BMW's
most ambitious platform overhaul in two decades. The role demands a leader who can
operate at the intersection of legacy automotive engineering and Silicon Valley-speed
software delivery.

Key Responsibilities

- Define and execute a 5-year technology roadmap for EV drivetrain, SDV middleware,
  and connected services, aligning with the NEUE KLASSE programme timeline.
- Lead the integration of the Autonomy.AI acquisition into BMW's R&D structure,
  harmonising engineering practices, toolchains, and culture across Munich, Tel Aviv,
  and Shenzhen.
- Manage a P&L exceeding EUR 550M, ensuring investment discipline while protecting
  critical innovation programmes.
- Build and retain a world-class engineering organisation of 250+ across software,
  electrical architecture, and applied AI, in a competitive talent market.
- Partner with the Chief Financial Officer, Chief Operating Officer, and regional
  heads to align technology investments with commercial priorities across EMEA and
  APAC markets.
- Represent BMW Group's technology vision to regulators, industry bodies, and
  strategic partners (chipmakers, cloud providers, ADAS suppliers).
- Champion a culture of engineering excellence that balances BMW's consensus-oriented
  decision-making tradition with the agility required for software delivery cycles.
- Establish robust cybersecurity and data-privacy frameworks for connected-vehicle
  services compliant with UNECE WP.29 and EU Cyber Resilience Act.

Required Qualifications

- 12+ years of progressive technology leadership experience in automotive, mobility,
  or adjacent deep-tech sectors (autonomous systems, robotics, semiconductors), with
  at least 5 years at VP/SVP level or equivalent.
- Demonstrated experience managing a P&L of USD 500M+ (or equivalent) and leading
  engineering organisations of 200+ people across multiple geographies.
- Deep technical fluency in at least two of: EV powertrain architecture, SDV
  middleware (AUTOSAR Adaptive, Android Automotive, or equivalent), ADAS/AD perception
  stacks, vehicle cybersecurity.
- Track record of successful post-acquisition technology integration — harmonising
  teams, tech stacks, and delivery cadences across legacy and startup cultures.
- Experience operating in premium automotive or tier-1 supplier environments; strong
  understanding of automotive product development cycles (V-model, ASPICE).
- Direct accountability for technology delivery in both EMEA and APAC markets,
  including familiarity with China-specific regulatory, data-localisation, and
  partnership requirements.
- MBA, MS, or PhD in engineering, computer science, or a related technical discipline
  from a top-tier institution.
- Professional fluency in English (business language) and German (working language
  for Board-level interactions); additional languages a plus.

Desired Attributes

- Proven ability to navigate complex stakeholder landscapes involving board members,
  works councils, regulators, and external technology partners.
- Comfort operating in a consensus-driven Germanic corporate culture while driving
  urgency on software delivery timelines.
- Passion for digital transformation and the vision to bridge legacy automotive
  engineering and modern software-defined product development.
- Track record of leading large-scale digital transformation programmes spanning
  multiple business units and geographies.
""".strip()
